<title>SPAIN: Spain's SEPI names Endesa sale coordinators.</title>
<headline>Spain's SEPI names Endesa sale coordinators.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's state holding SEPI said on Monday it had named Spanish bank Argentaria, Santander Investment -- a unit of Banco Santander -- and Merrill Lynch as global coordinators for the upcoming privatisation of the Spain's electrical company Endesa.</p>
<p>The statement added that the final details and design of the share sale would be set in October.  </p>
<p>SEPI said the size of the stake would be announced only when the privatisation project was ready.</p>
<p>SEPI now has 66.89 percent of Endesa, with 173.93 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
